# Agreeing on a signature that loads proves little: the canonical document is
# close to the file, so two readers can produce the same bytes while
# understanding nothing. Agreeing on what to refuse is the evidence, because
# refusing requires knowing what each field meant.
#
# Each case breaks exactly one thing that a typing defect would otherwise let
# through into a wrong application. Diagnostic prose is not compared — the ids
# are the contract and the reference has none to offer.
#
# REQUIRES: uv
# RUN: %uv python %S/Inputs/signature_mutations.py \
# RUN:   %zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json zkc-registry-lint \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s
# The control is asserted, not merely run: a non-zero exit is evidence of
# refusal only while the tool is known to admit something, so deleting the
# control has to break this test rather than quietly weaken it.
# CHECK: control: the unmutated signature admits
# CHECK: 79/79 refused by both
